\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Happy are they, they that love God,
\par Whose hearts have Christ confest, 
\par Who by His Cross have found their life,
\par And 'neath His yoke their rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Glad is the praise, sweet are the songs,
\par When they together sing;
\par And strong the prayers that bow the ear
\par Of heaven's eternal Kin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Christ to their homes giveth His peace,
\par And makes their loves His own;
\par But ah, what tares the evil one
\par Hath in His garden sown.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Sad were our lot, evil this earth,
\par Did not its sorrows prove
\par The path whereby the sheep may find
\par The fold of Jesus' love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then shall they know, they halt love Him,
\par How all their pain is good;
\par And death itself cannot unbind
\par Their happy brotherhood.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

